tuxcards-qt6 (3.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Editor: in-entry find / replace bar (Ctrl+F / Ctrl+H), embedded
    at the bottom of the editor. Tree-wide search moved to
    Ctrl+Shift+F to free Ctrl+F for the editor (standard convention).
    Case-sensitive + whole-word options, wrap-around, F3 / Shift+F3
    for next/previous match, browser-style behaviour for Replace.
  * Encryption: optional lazy-decrypt mode (Options → Encryption →
    "Decrypt entries only when viewed"). When enabled, opening an
    encrypted file only verifies the password against one entry —
    the rest stay in ciphertext until you click on them. Useful for
    large encrypted trees where decrypting everything on open is
    perceptibly slow. The cross-tree Search dialog now reports how
    many entries it had to skip in this mode.

 -- gzivdo <gzivdo@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 16 May 2026 18:00:00 +0000

tuxcards-qt6 (3.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Crypto:
    - Save no longer freezes the UI on encrypted files — eliminated
      a redundant per-element decrypt() during save, and added a
      session key cache so PBKDF2 / Argon2i runs once per save burst
      instead of once per element.
    - New optional XChaCha20-Poly1305 + Argon2i crypto backend via
      vendored monocypher (no external dependency). Selectable at
      build time with -DTUXCARDS_WRITE_BACKEND=openssl|monocypher;
      AES-256-GCM remains the default for new writes. Reader
      auto-detects format by magic header, so both backends coexist.
    - StringCrypter::clearKeyCache() is wired in MainWindow on file
      open/close/clearAll to bound how long the derived key sits in
      memory.

 -- gzivdo <gzivdo@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 16 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000

tuxcards-qt6 (3.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging-only follow-up to 3.1.0:
    - One .deb per supported Debian/Ubuntu release
      (ubuntu24.04, ubuntu26.04, debian12, debian13), each with
      Depends: lines resolved against that distro's own Qt6/OpenSSL.
    - Disable Fedora -debuginfo / -debugsource sub-packages.
    - install(TARGETS) now declares a BUNDLE destination so the
      macOS .app builds cleanly.

 -- gzivdo <gzivdo@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 16 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

tuxcards-qt6 (3.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bookmarks toolbar + back-ported CRecentFileList from 2.2.1.
  * AES-256-GCM + PBKDF2-SHA256 file encryption (legacy Blowfish format
    still readable).
  * CMake build alongside qmake; .deb / .rpm / Windows zip / macOS dmg
    artifacts produced by GitHub Actions on tag.
  * Auto-save status indicator, Markdown export/import.
  * QTest unit tests under tests/.
  * i18n for 10 languages (en, ru fully translated; de/zh_CN/zh_TW/es/
    fr/pt_BR/ja/ko skeletons).

 -- gzivdo <gzivdo@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 16 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

